      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bright%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Since the 1980s, Bright has shifted from a small rural community to an exurb of Cincinnati, reflecting suburban growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bright%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bright sits in northeastern Dearborn County, spanning Logan, Harrison, and Miller townships, a unique tri‑township arrangement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bright%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The eastern edge of Bright’s census‑designated place follows the Indiana–Ohio border, placing it right on the state line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bright%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Phantom Bridge, built in 1917 over the Whitewater River, was bypassed in the 1930s when State Route 1 was realigned.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historyinyourownbackyard.com/city/bright-indiana/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
